in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @cascade
in @labeled
in @facet/turing
in @facet/mirror

# @cascade/code/turing/mirror — the Turing tape → mirror substrate
# value cascade species.
#
# Path naming: per Alex 2026-06-23 directive — cascade species
# shards group by `@cascade/code/<source>/<target>`. Source
# language (Turing tape) groups together at
# `shards/cascade/code/turing/`; target (mirror here; potentially
# other targets in future arcs) leafs at
# `shards/cascade/code/turing/mirror.mirror`.
#
# THIS species is Edge 3 of the concrete polyglot chain Alex
# ratified 2026-07-17 (verbatim, session-crystallizing):
#
#   *"So we can have @cascade/code/llvm/turing and
#    @cascade/code/rust/llvm. And boom. The loop closes."*
#
# The full chain per polyglot spec §4.1 (Mara `1ce68c3`,
# 2026-07-17):
#
#   Rust source
#     ↓  @cascade/code/rust/llvm      (sibling mint this tick)
#   LLVM IR
#     ↓  @cascade/code/llvm/turing    (sibling mint this tick)
#   Turing tape
#     ↓  @cascade/code/turing/mirror  (THIS shard; tape → mirror
#                                       substrate composition)
#   mirror substrate composition
#
# === substrate-already-had-the-word ===
#
# Per Alex 2026-07-17 verbatim (polyglot spec §4.2 Edge 3
# grounding):
#
#   *"mirror itself treats tapes as just one linear serialization
#    target"*
#
# The mirror substrate ALREADY consumes tape-shaped byte-sequences
# as one of its landed linear-serialization forms (per
# `docs/specs/craft-binary-target.md` §"eight stages" — the
# concat stage consumes linear byte sequences; the store stage
# content-addresses them). THIS shard names the substrate-decl
# for tape-op consumption at cascade altitude — making the
# implicit tape-consumption explicit at family-root discipline.
#
# The FLOOR resolver (Reed Tick M3 domain) shells to substrate-
# native tape → mirror composition; each tape-op becomes a
# substrate fragment; state transitions become composition edges;
# the whole tape becomes a `@mirror/store`-content-addressed
# graph.
#
# === composition altitude: FLOOR ↔ SUBSTRATE-NATIVE ===
#
# The source altitude is `@facet/turing` (landed
# `shards/code/turing.mirror` this session; Mara M1 `7186410`) —
# the physical-substrate FLOOR per polyglot spec §2.3. The target
# altitude is `@facet/mirror` (landed `shards/code/mirror.mirror`
# 2026-06-07) — mirror's own instance of `@facet` at the mirror
# altitude.
#
# THIS cascade is the loop-closing edge: it lifts the Turing tape
# floor back into the substrate the compiler operates at. Per
# polyglot spec §3.2 composition axiom, THIS species composes
# with:
#
#   - `@cascade/code/llvm/turing` (sibling mint this tick) →
#     gives `@cascade/code/llvm/mirror` derived cascade.
#   - Chained further with `@cascade/code/rust/llvm` (sibling
#     mint this tick) → gives the full Rust → mirror loop-
#     closing composition Alex ratified.
#   - Composable via `@glue.compose` (per `shards/glue.mirror`)
#     with existing mirror substrate carriers (@glass, @nl,
#     @prism) at their own altitudes.
#
# === The cascade shape (Turing tape → mirror substrate value) ===
#
# Source (Turing tape admits per Church-Turing 1936 +
# `@facet/turing` M1):
# - linear symbol sequence (tape as `[symbol]`)
# - deterministic transition function (per Turing 1936 §1)
# - finite state-set (per `turing_well_formed`)
# - finite alphabet (per `turing_well_formed`)
# - halt-state enumeration
# - reachability graph (transitive closure of transitions per
#   `configuration_reachable` bilateral)
#
# Target (mirror substrate preserves per @facet/mirror + @mirror/
# store):
# - content-addressed graph nodes (OID-typed refs per
#   @mirror/store discipline)
# - composition edges (per @glue.compose morphism composition)
# - typed carriers (per @glass verdict + @nl language surface +
#   @prism five-op discipline)
# - substrate-native composition (per @facet/mirror's
#   grammar/render sub-species)
# - identity-contract preservation (byte-equality on OID)
#
# Per polyglot spec §4.4 Edge 3:
# - PRESERVED: computational semantics (every tape-op has a
#   substrate-decl'd equivalent), reachability graph, halt
#   conditions.
# - LOST: (potentially) the tape's linear-address discipline —
#   mirror's content-addressed graph altitude doesn't have linear
#   addresses; the cascade must reify tape-positions as
#   edge-labels.
#
# The `loss_lens<@facet/turing, @facet/mirror>` measures these gaps
# against the Turing 1936 tape model + mirror's substrate-decl
# graph altitude.
#
# === How mirror consumes tape as substrate value ===
#
# Per polyglot spec §4.2 Edge 3: "tape-op → mirror composition —
# `mirror` consumes tape ops as one linear serialization form."
# Concrete substrate-consumption:
#
#   1. Each `@facet/turing.symbol` on the tape becomes a substrate
#      fragment (content-addressed ref per @mirror/store).
#   2. Each `@facet/turing.state` becomes a composition node in
#      the mirror graph (typed carrier per @glass discipline).
#   3. Each `@facet/turing.transition` becomes a composition edge
#      (morphism per @glue.compose shape at
#      `shards/glue.mirror`).
#   4. Each `@facet/turing.head_position` becomes an edge label
#      (mirror has no linear addresses; positions reify as
#      graph-edge annotations).
#   5. The whole `@facet/turing.program` becomes a
#      `@mirror/store`-content-addressed graph.
#
# The resulting ref IS a mirror-native substrate value composable
# via `@glue.compose` (per Mara canonical @glue spec) with
# existing mirror substrate carriers (@glass verdicts, @nl
# strings, @prism five-op prisms).
#
# === Recognition ancestry ===
#
# - Recognition #95 (@cascade candidate; Mara canonical
#   `ce4874b`, 2026-06-23): this species IS one of the cascade
#   species discharging the family-root.
# - Recognition #93 H4 RESOLVED (labeled<> functor at
#   `shards/labeled.mirror`): mirror_artifact uses labeled<>
#   instance for substrate-value + consumption metadata.
# - Recognition #51 (mirror as expanding Hilbert space): the
#   dimension-projection from Turing tape's linear-symbol basis
#   to mirror's content-addressed-graph basis is measurable via
#   `measure_turing_mirror`; the projection REBASES the tape's
#   linear surface into mirror's graph altitude while preserving
#   computational semantics.
# - Recognition #104 chain P5 (@glue family-root at
#   `shards/glue.mirror`, Mara `fdcba31`): THIS cascade
#   discharges via `@glue.compose` to lift its outcome into the
#   mirror-substrate composition altitude; the composed outcome
#   participates in future @glue.translate invocations.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   Turing 1936               Alan Turing, "On Computable
#                             Numbers, with an Application to
#                             the Entscheidungsproblem", Proc.
#                             Lond. Math. Soc. s2-42:230-265.
#                             The source tape-model this species
#                             lifts.
#   Content-addressed         Merkle 1979 (dissertation);
#   storage                   git 2005; IPFS 2014. The substrate
#                             discipline @mirror/store implements
#                             and this cascade delivers into.
#   Category theory of        Mac Lane 1971 §I.1 categorical
#   composition               composition; the mathematical
#                             ground for @glue.compose lifting
#                             tape into graph altitude.
#   craft-binary-target.md    Reed 2026-05-19; the reverse-chain
#                             (mirror → LLVM → runnable) prior
#                             art; grounds mirror's ALREADY-
#                             LANDED tape-linear-consumption
#                             disposition at concat/store stages.
#
# Spec context: docs/specs/polyglot-loss-aware-computational-
#               translation.md §4.1 + §4.2 Edge 3 + §9 M2 (Mara
#               `1ce68c3`, 2026-07-17 — the mint plan
#               forward-promise THIS shard discharges); §4.4
#               Edge 3 preservation/loss enumeration; §1.1
#               verbatim on tape-as-linear-serialization-target
#               (Alex 2026-07-17). docs/specs/craft-binary-
#               target.md §"eight stages" (Reed 2026-05-19; the
#               empirical prior art for mirror's tape-linear
#               consumption at concat/store).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-lift-as-load-bearing]] (the
#                      lift is Alex's verbatim ratification +
#                      mirror's already-landed tape-linear-
#                      consumption at concat/store; NOT re-derived),
#                      [[feedback-loss-from-epistemologic-properties]]
#                      (loss is @epistemologic/properties composite,
#                      not Shannon, not invented),
#                      [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]] (every action
#                      body `\` blocked; FLOOR realisation domain).
# Related shards: shards/cascade.mirror (the family-root this
#                 specializes); shards/labeled.mirror (the functor
#                 primitive mirror_artifact instance rests on);
#                 shards/code/turing.mirror (source grammar; Mara
#                 M1 landed this session at `7186410`);
#                 shards/code/mirror.mirror (target grammar);
#                 shards/glue.mirror (the compose action THIS
#                 species discharges into; Mara `fdcba31`);
#                 shards/cascade/code/llvm/turing.mirror (sibling
#                 mint this tick; composes with THIS species per
#                 polyglot spec §3.2 to give LLVM → mirror).
# Path-namespace property: this file at
# `shards/cascade/code/turing/mirror.mirror` declares
# `@cascade/code/turing/mirror` per
# `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.

source @arxiv/theoretical-cs/turing-1936-computable-numbers

prism @cascade/code/turing/mirror {
  focus cascade
  project cascade
  split cascade
  shift cascade
  settle cascade
}

# === turing_source carrier ===
#
# Specialization of @cascade.typed_source for source_grammar=turing.
# References a `@facet/turing.program` as the unit of cascade. The
# substrate re-declares this carrier as an alias for the program
# type so the cascade action signatures type-check at the species
# altitude; the underlying identity is the program's content-
# addressed OID per @mirror/store discipline.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the program's content-
# addressed byte-form (transitions + initial_state + halt_states
# per Mara `7186410` `@facet/turing.program`).
type turing_source = program

# === mirror_consumption_metadata carrier ===
#
# Structured carrier for the tape → mirror consumption shape
# (position-to-edge-label mapping strategy, symbol-to-fragment
# encoding, state-to-node mapping, transition-to-morphism
# construction). Per [[feedback-no-bare-types]]: structured, not
# stringly. The carrier names load-bearing fields without fixing
# one consumption scheme; the FLOOR resolver (Reed Tick M3)
# populates concrete values from its Rust-native implementation
# of the tape-to-graph lifting per polyglot spec §4.2 Edge 3.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref.
type mirror_consumption_metadata = ref

# === mirror_artifact carrier ===
#
# The @labeled<> instance per recognition #93 H4. A
# mirror_artifact IS a mirror-substrate-value ref annotated with
# mirror_consumption_metadata via the labeled functor. Substrate-
# architecturally load-bearing: the substrate-value's typed
# identity is preserved (via labeled parametricity per Wadler
# 1989 / Reynolds 1983) while the consumption-scheme dimension
# is added. `unlabel(artifact)` returns the substrate-value;
# `label_of(artifact)` returns the metadata.
#
# The underlying substrate-value is a `ref` (content-addressed
# per @mirror/store discipline; composable via `@glue.compose`
# with existing mirror substrate carriers at their own altitudes).
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the (substrate-value,
# metadata) pair (inherited from @labeled).
type mirror_artifact = labeled(ref, mirror_consumption_metadata)

# === apply_turing_mirror action ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING ACTION. Specialization of @cascade.compile for
# the Turing tape → mirror substrate value functor. Takes a
# `@facet/turing.program`; returns a mirror-native substrate value
# (ref content-addressed per @mirror/store).
#
# Per Alex 2026-07-17 verbatim (polyglot spec §1.1 grounding):
# *"mirror itself treats tapes as just one linear serialization
# target"*. The realisation lifts the tape into mirror's graph
# altitude per polyglot spec §4.2 Edge 3 five-step consumption:
#
#   1. Each symbol → substrate fragment (content-addressed ref).
#   2. Each state → composition node (typed carrier).
#   3. Each transition → composition edge (morphism per
#      @glue.compose).
#   4. Each head_position → edge label (reified since mirror
#      has no linear addresses).
#   5. Whole program → @mirror/store-content-addressed graph.
#
# The FLOOR resolver (Reed Tick M3 under
# `[substrate-floor:@io-boundary]`) MUST discharge the body in
# Rust; THIS shard names the CONTRACT the FLOOR honors.
#
# requires turing_well_formed(prog): the source program MUST pass
# `@facet/turing.turing_well_formed` per Mara `7186410`.
# Ill-formed tape programs cannot be lifted into mirror
# substrate; the well-formedness bilateral gates the cascade.
#
# The result is composable via `@glue.compose` (per
# `shards/glue.mirror`) with existing mirror substrate carriers.
#
# Body discharges at the FLOOR boundary.
apply_turing_mirror(prog: program, p: perturbation) -> ref
requires turing_well_formed(prog)
{ \ }

# === bundle_mirror action ===
#
# Wraps a mirror-substrate-value ref + mirror_consumption_metadata
# into a mirror_artifact via @labeled.label construction. The
# typed substrate-value gets the consumption-scheme dimension
# added without losing the underlying substrate-value identity.
#
# requires mirror_consumption_coherent(substrate_value, metadata, p):
# bilateral commitment that the (substrate-value, metadata) pair
# coheres at the tape-to-graph consumption altitude — position-
# to-edge-label mapping consistent; symbol-to-fragment encoding
# reversible; state-to-node mapping bijective; transition-to-
# morphism construction discharges via @glue.compose.
#
# Body discharges at the FLOOR boundary.
bundle_mirror(substrate_value: ref, metadata: mirror_consumption_metadata, p: perturbation)
  -> mirror_artifact
requires mirror_consumption_coherent(substrate_value, metadata, p)
{ \ }

# === measure_turing_mirror action ===
#
# Specialization of @cascade.measure for the Turing tape → mirror
# substrate cascade. Returns substrate-typed measurement of
# information loss between turing_source's linear-symbol tape
# surface and mirror_artifact's content-addressed-graph structure.
#
# Returns `imperfect<mirror_artifact, ref, information_loss>` —
# the loss slot carries measured loss as substrate-typed data,
# NOT Shannon, NOT estimation; the composite of @epistemologic/
# properties per [[feedback-loss-from-epistemologic-properties]].
#
# The measurement IS substrate-architectural: read source's tape
# structure (symbol count, state count, transition count, halt-
# state enumeration, head-position range); read artifact's graph
# structure (node count, edge count, edge-label reification
# count, content-addressed-fragment count); compute the dimension
# gap per polyglot spec §4.4 Edge 3 preservation/loss enumeration.
#
# Substrate-honest note: this cascade's loss profile is
# ARCHITECTURALLY SHALLOW — Turing tape and mirror substrate
# are both Turing-complete altitudes; the primary loss is the
# linear-address discipline reification, not computational
# semantics.
#
# requires turing_mirror_loss_well_defined(prog, artifact, p):
# bilateral that the measurement IS computable; the (program,
# artifact) pair must be a genuine cascade discharge.
#
# Body discharges at the FLOOR boundary.
measure_turing_mirror(prog: program, artifact: mirror_artifact, p: perturbation)
  -> imperfect(mirror_artifact, ref, information_loss)
requires turing_mirror_loss_well_defined(prog, artifact, p)
{ \ }

# === mirror_consumption_coherent bilateral ===
#
# Target-side consumption-well-formedness bilateral. Commitment
# that the (substrate-value, metadata) pair coheres at the tape-
# to-graph consumption altitude.
#
# Splinter-pole: position-to-edge-label mapping consistent
# across all reified positions; symbol-to-fragment encoding
# reversible (fragment OID → symbol byte-form retrievable);
# state-to-node mapping bijective (each state corresponds to
# exactly one graph node); transition-to-morphism construction
# discharges via @glue.compose; substrate-value composable with
# existing @glass/@nl/@prism carriers.
# Narcissus-pole: mapping inconsistency; encoding non-reversible;
# state-node correspondence broken (multiple states → one node
# OR one state → multiple nodes); morphism construction fails
# @glue.compose discharge; substrate-value incomposable at
# @glass/@nl/@prism altitude.

bilateral mirror_consumption_coherent {
  sentinel "consumption=position-symbol-state-morphism-coherent"
  arity 2
}
mirror_consumption_coherent(substrate_value: ref, metadata: mirror_consumption_metadata, p: perturbation)
  -> verdict { \ }

# === turing_mirror_loss_well_defined bilateral ===
#
# Specializes the family-root's loss_well_defined for this
# cascade. Commitment that the substrate-typed gap calculation IS
# computable for the (program, artifact) pair; the program IS in
# @facet/turing grammar (well-formed), the artifact's substrate-
# value IS content-addressed per @mirror/store discipline, and
# the pair represents a valid cascade discharge
# (`apply_turing_mirror` produced THIS artifact from THIS program).
#
# Splinter-pole: cascade-pair coherent; measurement well-defined;
# gap dimensions dischargeable per @epistemologic/properties
# composite.
# Narcissus-pole: source/artifact grammar mismatch OR pair does
# not represent a genuine cascade discharge; measurement
# undefined.

bilateral turing_mirror_loss_well_defined {
  sentinel "cascade=source-artifact-pair-discharge-witnessed"
  arity 2
}
turing_mirror_loss_well_defined(prog: program, artifact: mirror_artifact, p: perturbation)
  -> verdict { \ }

# === cascade_turing_mirror_admissible bilateral ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING composed bilateral for THIS species. Witnesses
# that the Turing tape → mirror substrate cascade produces a
# mirror-substrate-consumable outcome — that is, the resulting
# ref IS composable via @glue.compose with existing mirror
# substrate carriers at their own altitudes (@glass verdicts,
# @nl strings, @prism five-op prisms).
#
# Per Alex 2026-07-17 verbatim ratification: mirror ALREADY
# treats tapes as one linear serialization target; the cascade
# lifts the tape into mirror's graph altitude such that the
# outcome participates in mirror substrate composition natively.
# The admissibility check is whether the outcome IS substrate-
# consumable at the mirror altitude — not a semantic-preservation
# claim (that's discharged at earlier edges), but a substrate-
# composition claim.
#
# Splinter-pole: mirror_artifact.substrate_value IS content-
# addressed per @mirror/store; IS composable via @glue.compose
# with @glass/@nl/@prism carriers; participates natively in
# mirror substrate composition; no pre-processing required by
# downstream consumers.
# Narcissus-pole: substrate-value not properly content-
# addressed; @glue.compose discharge fails; incomposable with
# mirror-native carriers; downstream consumers require ad-hoc
# lifting.
#
# Sentinel `cascade=mirror-substrate-consumable` per Mara
# `701828a` §1 byte-containment: content-addressed check on the
# cascade-outcome OID vs the substrate-consumption invariant.
# Rice-safe per Mara `701828a` — the CHECK is byte-level; the
# check discharges by structural inspection of the outcome ref's
# composability with @glue.compose signature (per
# `shards/glue.mirror`).

bilateral cascade_turing_mirror_admissible {
  sentinel "cascade=mirror-substrate-consumable"
  arity 1
}
cascade_turing_mirror_admissible(cascade_outcome: mirror_artifact) -> verdict { \ }

# === turing_mirror_cascade_well_formed composed bilateral ===
#
# Specialization of @cascade.cascade_well_defined for this cascade
# instance. Composes the sub-predicates at this altitude per the
# landed cascade composed-bilateral shape.
#
# requires turing_well_formed(prog): source tape program passes
# @facet/turing.turing_well_formed per Mara `7186410`.
# requires mirror_consumption_coherent(unlabel(artifact, p),
# label_of(artifact, p), p): target-side consumption well-formed;
# uses @labeled.unlabel + @labeled.label_of to extract substrate-
# value and metadata from the artifact.
# requires turing_mirror_loss_well_defined(prog, artifact, p):
# loss measurement computable.
# requires cascade_turing_mirror_admissible(artifact): outcome
# mirror-substrate-consumable per @glue.compose composability.
#
# All four must hold; substrate refuses cascade if source tape
# program ill-formed OR consumption incoherent OR loss undefined
# OR outcome not mirror-substrate-consumable.
#
# Splinter-pole: all four discharge; substrate-typed loss
# returned; cascade admissible per polyglot spec §5.3
# threshold gate; outcome enters mirror substrate composition
# natively.
# Narcissus-pole: at least one sub-predicate fails; cascade
# blocked; @fate re-selects per polyglot spec §6.

bilateral turing_mirror_cascade_well_formed {
  sentinel "cascade=all-sub-bilaterals-discharge"
  arity 2
}
turing_mirror_cascade_well_formed(prog: program, artifact: mirror_artifact, p: perturbation)
  -> verdict
requires turing_well_formed(prog)
requires mirror_consumption_coherent(unlabel(artifact, p), label_of(artifact, p), p)
requires turing_mirror_loss_well_defined(prog, artifact, p)
requires cascade_turing_mirror_admissible(artifact)
{ \ }

# === outbound declarations ===

out @cascade/code/turing/mirror
out turing_source
out mirror_consumption_metadata
out mirror_artifact
out apply_turing_mirror
out bundle_mirror
out measure_turing_mirror
out mirror_consumption_coherent
out turing_mirror_loss_well_defined
out cascade_turing_mirror_admissible
out turing_mirror_cascade_well_formed
